From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:25:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: hdmi: Let DRM manage the encoder and its memory

sun4i_drv no longer calls drm_mode_config_cleanup() itself (drm/sun4i:
drv: Do not call drm_mode_config_cleanup()). The managed release of
drm_mode_config_init() destroys the mode objects at the last
drm_dev_put() instead, after component_unbind_all(), and, while
userspace still holds the device open, after the display engine device
has released its devres.

The HDMI encoder and connector live in devm memory of the HDMI device,
which component_unbind_all() frees before that, so they are cleaned up
on freed memory even without a file open. The connector is already
managed (drmm_connector_hdmi_init()), the encoder is not.

Allocate struct sun4i_hdmi with drmm_kzalloc() and initialise the
encoder with drmm_encoder_init(); the managed actions clean up the
connector and the encoder, in that order, before the memory is freed.
The managed variant wants a NULL .destroy, so drop the hook, and the
error path no longer cleans up the encoder by hand.

Not covered: the HDMI DDC and TMDS clocks and the I2C adapter, which
stay in the devres of the HDMI device and go with it.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: not tested; the board has no controller of
this kind, the code is compiled only.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_enc.c | 12 ++++--------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_enc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_enc.c
index 97253d631b2b..565a534c4dea 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_enc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_hdmi_enc.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <drm/drm_atomic_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_edid.h>
 #include <drm/drm_encoder.h>
+#include <drm/drm_managed.h>
 #include <drm/drm_of.h>
 #include <drm/drm_panel.h>
 #include <drm/drm_print.h>
@@ -171,10 +172,6 @@ static void sun4i_hdmi_enable(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
 	writel(val, hdmi->base + SUN4I_HDMI_VID_CTRL_REG);
 }
 
-static const struct drm_encoder_funcs sun4i_hdmi_funcs = {
-	.destroy = drm_encoder_cleanup,
-};
-
 static const struct drm_encoder_helper_funcs sun4i_hdmi_helper_funcs = {
 	.atomic_disable	= sun4i_hdmi_disable,
 	.atomic_enable	= sun4i_hdmi_enable,
@@ -514,7 +511,7 @@ static int sun4i_hdmi_bind(struct device *dev, struct device *master,
 	u32 reg;
 	int ret;
 
-	hdmi = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*hdmi), GFP_KERNEL);
+	hdmi = drmm_kzalloc(drm, sizeof(*hdmi), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!hdmi)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	dev_set_drvdata(dev, hdmi);
@@ -627,8 +624,8 @@ static int sun4i_hdmi_bind(struct device *dev, struct device *master,
 
 	drm_encoder_helper_add(&hdmi->encoder,
 			       &sun4i_hdmi_helper_funcs);
-	ret = drm_encoder_init(drm, &hdmi->encoder, &sun4i_hdmi_funcs,
-			       DRM_MODE_ENCODER_TMDS, NULL);
+	ret = drmm_encoder_init(drm, &hdmi->encoder, NULL,
+				DRM_MODE_ENCODER_TMDS, NULL);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "Couldn't initialise the HDMI encoder\n");
 		goto err_put_ddc_i2c;
@@ -687,7 +684,6 @@ static int sun4i_hdmi_bind(struct device *dev, struct device *master,
 
 err_cleanup_connector:
 	cec_delete_adapter(hdmi->cec_adap);
-	drm_encoder_cleanup(&hdmi->encoder);
 err_put_ddc_i2c:
 	i2c_put_adapter(hdmi->ddc_i2c);
 err_del_i2c_adapter:
